WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.200
NARRATOR: In this
video, we're going

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.700
to walk through how
to manage member

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.130
permissions for your Google
Cloud billing account.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.050
To manage member
permissions, you'll

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.720
need to be a Billing Account
Administrator on the billing

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.380
account.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.630
Get started by heading
into the Console,

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.720
then head to the Navigation
menu in the left-hand pane.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.070
Choose Billing.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.820
Then use the drop-down menu to
select Manage Billing Accounts.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.500
Select the billing
account for which

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.990
you'd like to manage
members and permissions.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.390
This will open
the Overview page.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.630
In the left hand nav,
choose Account Management.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.790
To the right, you will
see the info panel

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.830
where you can view the
list of current members,

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.570
edit their permissions,
or remove them.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.330
You can also add new members.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:47.420
Permissions are bundled to
form several functional roles.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.960
Billing Account Administrators
can view cost information, link

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.060
and unlink projects
from the account,

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.520
and manage other member
roles on the account.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.130
They are also the only
ones who can contact Google

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.870
Cloud support if you need help.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:02.900
Billing Account Costs
Managers can view all cost

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.510
details, including project costs
and non-project related costs,

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:09.170
such as the cost of
support or subscriptions.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.260
They can also manage budgets
and export cost information

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.300
to BigQuery for analysis.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.790
Billing Account Viewers
can view all cost details

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:20.000
for the billing account and
view, but not edit, budgets

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.100
and BigQuery export settings.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.320
Billing Account Users
can link projects

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.180
with the billing account.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:29.610
These role assignments are made
at the billing account level.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.910
However, there are also
billing-related roles

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:35.450
at the organization,
folder, and project levels.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.160
You can set roles
at these levels

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.280
by navigating to the project,
folder, or organization

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.760
from the project selector,
and then to the IAM page,

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.350
where you can view
current members

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:48.020
and add new members and roles.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.440
At the project or folder
level, Project Billing Managers

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.330
can assign a project's
billing account

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:56.360
when they have the billing
account user role on the target

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.680
billing account.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.590
They can also disable
a project's billing.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:03.530
At the organization level,
Billing Account Creators

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:06.320
can create new self-serve
billing accounts.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.870
It is a good idea to minimize
the number of members

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:11.000
who have this role in
order to better manage

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.100
your organization's
billing accounts and spend.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.930
You can also set the roles
that we discussed earlier,

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.770
such as Billing Account
Administrator, User, and Viewer

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.960
at the organization
level and the permissions

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.840
will apply to all the Cloud
billing accounts, projects,

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.970
and resources in
the organization.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:30.980
Head over to the documentation
to check out more details.

